# s710_security_part2.oot — (Part 2 of s710_security.oot)
# Continuation of `openOODA/audit/s710_security.oot`.

## Attack results (product host)
Verdict key:

- **BLOCK** = emit-c **and** check `ERR\tsecret` + rc≠0 (llvm when run)
- **ALLOW** = both rc=0, no `ERR\tsecret` (correct for pass / non-tag)
- **FN** = allowed when a real line-start SECRET name reached a sink
- **FP** = refused when `SECRET:` was not a line-start directive
- **TRUNC** = refuse line names a prefix/suffix, not the full ident

Host: `OODAC=/home/jeryd/Projects/openOODA/ooda/oodac/oodac`
Probes: `/tmp/s710_sec_M6VBmS/` (ephemeral).
Harness: `ooda/scripts/s710_parse_secret_env_smoke.oo` **exit 0**.

### Z1 — slice / extract must not drop or truncate
Source close (L43–65):

```
let start = k;
while is_al { k = k + 1 }
let name = str_slice(src, start, k);   # exclusive [start, k)
```

`k` is the first non-alnum/`_` or EOF. Same span the old concat loop
would have built. Ident class is still `_` / A–Z / a–z / 0–9 from the
**first** char (not 7.1 `is_start`). No stack buffer. No max length.

| # | Shape | emit-c | check | llvm | Trunc? |
|---|-------|--------|-------|------|--------|
| 1 | `// SECRET: api_key` → `println(api_key)` | rc=1 SECRET **api_key** | rc=1 SECRET **api_key** | rc=1 SECRET **api_key** | **no** |
| 2 | `_tok` | SECRET **_tok** | SECRET **_tok** | — | **no** |
| 3 | `API_Key_v2` | SECRET **API_Key_v2** | SECRET **API_Key_v2** | — | **no** |
| 4 | `key123` | SECRET **key123** | SECRET **key123** | — | **no** |
| 5 | `// SECRET:tok` (no space) | SECRET **tok** | SECRET **tok** | — | **no** |
| 6 | `// SECRET:<TAB>tok` | SECRET **tok** | SECRET **tok** | — | **no** |
| 7 | `// SECRET: tok extra junk` | SECRET **tok** (span stops) | SECRET **tok** | — | **no** |
| 8 | directive after `main` (EOF line) | SECRET **tok** | SECRET **tok** | — | **no** |
| 9 | two names; sink `beta_name` | SECRET **beta_name** | SECRET **beta_name** | — | **no** |
| 10 | `// SECRET: api-key` then `println(api)` | SECRET **api** | SECRET **api** | — | **no** (hyphen not `is_al`) |
| L32–L2048 | ident length 32 / 64 / 128 / 256 / 512 / 1024 / **2048** | SECRET full name | — | 128: full | **no** |
| F | `fixtures/secret_sink_fail` (`x`) | SECRET **x** | cache OK (R3) | — | **no** (emit) |
| F | `fixtures/secret_multi_name_fail` (`b`) | SECRET **b** | SECRET **b** | — | **no** |
| H | `s710_parse_secret_env_smoke` two-name a/b | SECRET a **and** SECRET b | — | — | **no** |

Python measure of refuse line vs written ident: **32…2048 all
`refused_len == name_len` and `refused == name`.** TRUNC count: **0**.

Why OOB empty cannot fire on this slice: `start` is `k` after the
space-skip; `k` only advances while `k < sn`; `start <= k <= sn`.
`oo_str_slice` empty-on-OOB is therefore **dead** for this call. The
only live empty is `start == k` (no ident) — Z2.

`// SECRET: 123key` **does** tag `123key` (`is_al` includes leading
digits). Lexer will not produce IDENT `123key`; sink was `println(x)`
→ ALLOW (unused tag). Pre-existing class; **not** a truncate FN. Do
not “fix” to 7.1 `is_start` in this close.

### Z2 — empty ident must not fail-open
Caller (source, must stay):

```
if name == "" {
    println("ERR\tsecret\tinvalid name (need ident after SECRET directive)");
    process_exit(1);
}
```

There is **no** `if name != "" { put; continue }`. Empty is fatal.

| # | Shape | emit-c | check | llvm | Verdict |
|---|-------|--------|-------|------|---------|
| 1 | `// SECRET:` (fixture `secret_invalid_empty`) | invalid name | invalid name | — | **BLOCK** |
| 2 | `// SECRET:` (ephemeral) | invalid name | invalid name | invalid name | **BLOCK** |
| 3 | `// SECRET:   ` spaces only | invalid name | invalid name | — | **BLOCK** |
| 4 | `// SECRET:<TABs>` | invalid name | invalid name | — | **BLOCK** |
| 5 | `// SECRET: !notident` | invalid name | invalid name | — | **BLOCK** |
| 6 | `// SECRET: -foo` | invalid name | invalid name | — | **BLOCK** |
| H | smoke `empty_name.oo` | invalid name | — | — | **BLOCK** |

**Empty-skip fail-open count: 0.**

Preamble prints **before** parse (`c_emit.oo` HITL/preamble, llvm
preamble). rc is still ≠0 and the last line is `ERR\tsecret\tinvalid
name`. Not a fail-open.

### Z3 — non-line-start `SECRET:` is not a directive
Line-start oracle (unchanged):

```
at_line = (i == 0) || (char_at(src, i-1) == "\n")
needle  = "// " + "SECRET:"     # exact, including the space
```

Only then: skip ` ` / `\t`, slice ident.

| # | Shape | emit-c | check | llvm | Tagged? |
|---|-------|--------|-------|------|---------|
| 1 | `// Mention // SECRET: leaked …` (`secret_midline_safe`) | rc=0 | rc=0 | — | **no** |
| 2 | same ephemeral midline | rc=0, no secret | rc=0 | rc=0 | **no** |
| 3 | `let leaked = "token"; // SECRET: leaked` | rc=0, no secret | rc=0 | — | **no** |
| 4 | `let leaked = "// SECRET: leaked"` | rc=0, no secret | rc=0 | — | **no** |
| 5 | indented `  // SECRET: leaked` | rc=0, no secret | rc=0 | rc=0 | **no** |
| 6 | `//SECRET: leaked` (no space after `//`) | rc=0, no secret | rc=0 | — | **no** |
| 7 | `// secret: leaked` (case) | rc=0, no secret | rc=0 | — | **no** |
| 8 | `SECRET: leaked` (not a comment) | parse IDENT | parse IDENT | — | **no** (not secret) |
| 9 | `/* SECRET: leaked */` | parse SLASH | parse SLASH | — | **no** (not secret) |
| 10 | first line `// SECRET: leaked\r\n` (CRLF) | SECRET leaked | SECRET leaked | — | **yes** (i==0; intended) |
| 11 | CR-only before `// SECRET:` | lex CR | lex CR | — | n/a (not a secret FN) |

**FP (false tag) count: 0.** Mid-line / string / indent / `//SECRET:` /
case-fold do **not** refuse `println(leaked)`.

Column-0 is the product line-start (not `^[[:space:]]*`). Indented
`// SECRET:` is **not** a tag — T2 `secret_midline_safe` + Z3-5. That
is the specified gate, not a 7.10 FN. Residual: authors who indent
directives get no tag (named R2).

